#### Variation 4: Context Propagation for Legacy Services

**Use Case**: Monolithic legacy services (not instrumented with OpenTelemetry) participate in distributed workflows alongside microservices.

**Implementation**:
- API Gateway creates trace ID and propagates via custom HTTP header (`X-Trace-ID`)
- Legacy service extracts `X-Trace-ID` from request, includes in all logs
- Downstream microservices extract `X-Trace-ID`, convert to OpenTelemetry trace context
- Partial trace captured (microservices instrumented, legacy service logs correlated by trace ID)

**Benefits**:
- Enable distributed tracing before fully migrating to microservices
- Correlate legacy service logs with microservice traces using trace ID
- Gradual migration path (instrument services incrementally)

**Configuration**:
```java
// API Gateway (instrumented)
String traceId = Span.current().getSpanContext().getTraceId();
httpHeaders.set("X-Trace-ID", traceId);

// Legacy Service (not instrumented)
String traceId = request.getHeader("X-Trace-ID");
logger.info("Processing request traceId={}", traceId);

// Downstream Microservice (instrumented)
String legacyTraceId = request.getHeader("X-Trace-ID");
Span.current().setAttribute("legacy.trace_id", legacyTraceId);
```

